cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Diffuse: local-first device history for Apple platforms and Android"
message: >-
  If you use Diffuse, its snapshot schema, or its capability-driven diff
  model in academic or technical work, please cite this repository.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nguyen
    given-names: Son
    alias: hoangsonww
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-7806-068X"
  - name: "The Diffuse contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hoangsonww/Diffuse-Native-Apps"
url: "https://hoangsonww.github.io/Diffuse-Native-Apps/"
abstract: >-
  Diffuse is a local-first device-history product built as five genuinely
  native applications: macOS, iOS, iPadOS, and watchOS in Swift 6 and
  SwiftUI, and Android in Kotlin and Jetpack Compose. It captures
  structured, schema-carrying snapshots of a device, compares any two of
  them with a generic diff engine, and keeps every snapshot on the device
  that observed it. There is no account, no cloud backend, no sync
  protocol, and no telemetry. The two runtime families share no code; they
  interoperate only through schema-v1 JSON snapshots and golden diff
  fixtures. Every observed property carries a privacy classification, and
  export redaction is driven by that classification rather than by an
  allow list maintained by hand.
keywords:
